id=a52sxq_home_depth_clock
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: home-screen depth clock (off by default, switch in UN1CA UI settings)
author=kusti420
description=Draws a large clock on the home wallpaper between the background and the cut-out subject when the home wallpaper is a Samsung layered wallpaper (Gallery -> wallpaper editor). SpriteWallpaper's engine factory (c3.a.a) normally gives the home-only instance (which & 3 == 1) a FlattenLayeredPresenter (h3.d) that bakes all layers into one bitmap; with persist.sys.k4.home_depth_clock=1 HomeDepthClock.presenter() returns HomeClockPresenter instead, which loads the layers through the stock LayeredPresenter (h3.f, WallpaperManager asset file descriptors), flattens them into two screen-sized bitmaps split at the subject node and puts a ClockNode between them. A home+lock shared layered wallpaper (which & 3 == 3) keeps its BgCachableLayeredPresenter (the lock screen's own animation needs its layers); h3.a.e -> HomeDepthClock.afterBuild() inserts a gated ClockNode that draws only while the keyguard is gone and the display is ON (opt-in, persist.sys.k4.home_depth_clock_shared=1, until checked on a phone with a shared wallpaper). LayeredEngine (f3.a) onCreate/onVisibilityChanged/onDestroy keep an EngineState: a reload receiver (com.k4.homeclock.action.RELOAD, sender needs WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS) that rebuilds the sub engine in-process (stopSelf -> factory again, no process death), and an ACTION_TIME_TICK receiver only while visible with a clock (redraw only when the shown minute is stale; no per-frame drawing, no wakeups). Unset/0 = stock rendering; the only difference left is the idle reload receiver of the home engine. Tunables: persist.sys.k4.home_depth_clock_y = digit centre in % of screen height or auto, persist.sys.k4.home_depth_clock_color = white (default) / accent / #RRGGBB. Settings > UN1CA > UI settings gets "Home screen depth clock" + "Clock position" (Automatic / Top / Middle) + "Clock colour" (White / Theme colour), added by settings.sh from post_mods.sh. Signed with aosp_platform like every rebuilt APK; the signature patch maps that to the platform signature, and the app has no sharedUserId. Wallpaper & style (DressRoom, dressroom.sh, UNTESTED on device): the Home screen "Set as wallpaper" editor gets Depth clock / Position / Colour items in its bottom menu, a clock preview kept below the cut-out subject layer, and commits the choice to the same properties + RELOAD when the wallpaper is applied; the patched system DressRoom gets versionCode 1301035000 so a Galaxy Store update (which would shadow it) is dropped at boot and no longer offered.
